# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Database
#
# Local: the Postgres container from `docker compose up -d` (see README).
# Production: linking a Neon database to the Vercel project is enough — the
#             config also accepts the DATABASE_URL / POSTGRES_URL that the
#             integration injects, so this does not need setting by hand.
#             Use the pooled connection string (host contains "-pooler");
#             Neon requires TLS, so keep ?sslmode=require on the end.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
DATABASE_URI=postgresql://payload:payload@localhost:5434/onboarding_resources

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Payload
#
# Signs admin session cookies and hashes tokens. Changing it logs everyone out.
# Generate with: openssl rand -base64 32
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PAYLOAD_SECRET=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# File uploads (production only)
#
# Vercel's filesystem is read-only apart from an ephemeral /tmp, so uploaded
# wallpapers and icons must go to Blob storage. Create a store under
# Vercel -> Storage -> Blob; it sets this variable on the project for you.
#
# Leave this unset locally — Payload then writes to ./public/media instead,
# which needs no setup.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN=
